[rvn-ple] Never allocate the dead swizzle placeholders under the marlin pin

0052 made prepare_moe_nvfp4_layer_for_marlin drop w13_blockscale_swizzled /
w2_blockscale_swizzled just before repacking each layer. That bought the repack
~2.5x more headroom but the launch still OOMed inside it, because the release is
one layer too late: create_weights allocates those two parameters at model
construction, so all 48 MoE layers hold them through the whole weight load
(2 x scale bytes per layer; the RVN checkpoint stores 7.031 GiB of expert
scales as float8_e4m3fn, so 7.03 GiB of duplicates model-wide), and only the
current layer's 0.1465 GiB is free by the time that layer's repack asks for
800 MiB with 572 MiB to spare.

Nothing on the marlin path can ever read them. apply() resolves its tensors
through get_marlin_quant_info and returns early (modelopt_quant.py:2871-2872),
and the only in-tree readers -- the eager getattr defaults at
modelopt_quant.py:2944-2948 and the list literal at 2973-2977 -- sit behind the
cutedsl / flashinfer backend predicates that a marlin backend cannot satisfy.
So stop allocating them for that backend rather than sweeping them at load
entry: no extra pass over the modules, and the bytes are free before the first
shard is read instead of one layer at a time.

The predicate extends the guard the trtllm branch in this same block already
uses for the same reason, and keeps its convention of assigning None (the
class's "backend does not use this" marker, modelopt_quant.py:2371/2391), which
degrades to a None value instead of an AttributeError if a future path ever
reads the attribute. LIL and every cutlass / trtllm run stay byte-identical:
is_marlin() is False for their backends, so the allocation they get is
unchanged, and the getattr keeps the pre-existing defensive idiom used at
modelopt_quant.py:2477 and 2862 for backends where 0048's pin never fires.

--- a/python/sglang/srt/layers/quantization/modelopt_quant.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/layers/quantization/modelopt_quant.py
@@ -2367,7 +2367,18 @@
         # TRTLLM replaces blockscale_swizzled with an alias to weight_scale
         # during process_weights_after_loading, so skip the expensive
         # swizzle+allocate here to avoid GPU memory fragmentation
-        if self.enable_flashinfer_trtllm_moe:
+        # Marlin never reads them either: apply() resolves its tensors through
+        # get_marlin_quant_info, and the cutedsl readers that use them as
+        # getattr defaults are unreachable under a marlin backend. 0048 pins
+        # marlin for W4A16_NVFP4, so allocating them would keep 2 x scale bytes
+        # per MoE layer live for the whole process (7.03 GiB across the
+        # 48-layer RVN checkpoint) and that is what squeezed the first repack.
+        if (
+            self.enable_flashinfer_trtllm_moe
+            or getattr(
+                self, "_moe_runner_backend", get_moe_runner_backend()
+            ).is_marlin()
+        ):
             layer.w13_blockscale_swizzled = None
         else:
             layer.w13_blockscale_swizzled = Parameter(
@@ -2387,7 +2398,12 @@
         )
         layer.register_parameter("w2_weight_scale", w2_weight_scale)
 
-        if self.enable_flashinfer_trtllm_moe:
